on":{"commit_sha":"57ec1e6633c98533071db65763863f749a036939","position":"1795038493052460921-825be6e1-2451-40d6-bea6-cf3c636d5f7c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"2d82f9b4ccd9c22cb4ce67703722b27ce3ff67bbc5c4fd5bcf7acb47cc2733e0","event_uuid":"0b1317b8-6b79-417c-9a74-c142667e2ad1","position":{"commit_sha":"5b9056318fd81068ee1c3bdbf8ec2314a6cb078d","position":"1795038667234501189-0b1317b8-6b79-417c-9a74-c142667e2ad1"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"673ea17ea6bd4eb2c7fa6e86a2685731d17c63e3dee2b6eeb5aca57e2c98ab8b","event_uuid":"8da4c301-e8e9-4ae8-8030-88982e8113bd","position":{"commit_sha":"80e464562d25dec02177f015f90ed17d39379aa6","position":"1795039063926312153-8da4c301-e8e9-4ae8-8030-88982e8113bd"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"907aafe55967d12531fbc3beb4f98ac438af1ca68e444eabbcfcb0913a5c6e0e","event_uuid":"62e19b50-6c9e-4624-9131-fb449d9551d5","position":{"commit_sha":"80e464562d25dec02177f015f90ed17d39379aa6","position":"1795039063955638415-62e19b50-6c9e-4624-9131-fb449d9551d5"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1795037763359188043,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[],"description":"## Context / Problem\n`tests/unit/test_mcp_idle_heap_release.py::test_finished_background_job_does_not_keep_its_memory` fails on every `sweep (py3.14t)` run since it landed in 9beecb409ab: 13 of 13 runs from 43991050364 (2026-11-17) through 44390588952 (2026-11-18), always this one test, always 271-275 MiB kept (e.g. job 135106845268: baseline 2224 MiB, before release 2499 MiB, idle +272 MiB). The `sweep (py3.14)` leg on the same ubuntu runner and glibc passes in the same runs. It is deterministic, not flaky.\n\nRoot cause: the test's premise is glibc-arena behaviour. Its large `str` objects are allocated through `PyObject_Malloc`. In a GIL build that goes to glibc `malloc` for objects over 512 bytes, so `malloc_trim(0)` (`src/rebar/_mcp_health.py::release_freed_heap`) returns the freed pages. In the free-threaded build CPython routes `PyObject_Malloc` and `PyMem_Malloc` through its bundled mimalloc, which is required and cannot be disabled there (CPython 3.14 C-API docs, \"Memory Management\": default allocators table, and \"The mimalloc allocator\"). glibc `malloc_trim` cannot release mimalloc segments, so the freed ~274 MiB stays resident: the trim is a no-op for exactly the memory the test measures. The deployed MCP image is `python:3.12-slim` (GIL build, `infra/compose/Dockerfile.mcp`), so the production release path is unaffected; `sweep (py3.14t)` is an experimental, nonblocking leg.\n\n## Approach\nScope the memory test to the builds whose object memory glibc owns: skip it when `sysconfig.get_config_var(\"Py_GIL_DISABLED\")` is truthy, with a reason naming mimalloc. Add one sentence to `release_freed_heap`'s docstring stating that on free-threaded builds Python objects live in mimalloc, which `malloc_trim` does not govern. No change to the release mechanism itself: there is no public CPython API to collect mimalloc heaps, and no deployed image runs free-threaded. No config key, env var or flag.\n\nRejected: retrying or loosening the 64 MiB threshold (the retained amount equals the whole freed amount, so any threshold that passes would make the test meaningless); calling private mimalloc symbols through ctypes (unexported, version-fragile).\n\nPortability: test-only skip condition using `sysconfig`, available on every platform and interpreter; no subprocesses, fds, paths or signals.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/unit/test_mcp_idle_heap_release.py` \u2014 add the free-threaded skip to the memory test.\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_health.py` \u2014 docstring sentence on `release_freed_heap` only.\n\n## Testing\n- GIL builds: the memory test still runs and passes on the Linux CI cells (ubuntu py3.11-3.13) and `sweep (py3.14)`; macOS and Windows still skip it as before.\n- Free-threaded build: after merge, dispatch `gh workflow run test.yml --ref main`; in `sweep (py3.14t)` this test no longer fails (it is skipped with the mimalloc reason). Any other failure in that job is unrelated and gets its own ticket.\n- `make verify` green in the worktree.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Root cause identified with evidence (deterministic on free-threaded builds vs intermittent).\n- [ ] On the post-merge `sweep (py3.14t)` job the memory test no longer fails: it is skipped on the free-threaded build with a reason naming mimalloc, and it still runs on the GIL `sweep (py3.14)` leg. No retry-until-green and no loosened threshold.\n- [ ] `make verify` passes and the change lands through Gerrit with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/unit/test_mcp_idle_heap_release.py","reason":"skip memory test on free-threaded builds"},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_health.py","reason":"docstring note on mimalloc"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"8da4c301-e8e9-4ae8-8030-88982e8113bd","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["ci","flaky-or-platform"],"ticket_id":"27fa-79cf-59c7-4db6","ticket_type":"bug","title":"test_mcp_idle_heap_release fails on the py3.14t (free-threaded) sweep: idle process keeps ~272 MiB","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["a6c8c56a-0108-4509-9478-22fbe935f5da","2c76be53-9085-4f20-8d2a-6fa4367f04fd","dfe7f5cf-7d33-4ccd-83d3-4fdffdf5b6dd","825be6e1-2451-40d6-bea6-cf3c636d5f7c","0b1317b8-6b79-417c-9a74-c142667e2ad1","8da4c301-e8e9-4ae8-8030-88982e8113bd","62e19b50-6c9e-4624-9131-fb449d9551d5"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795039063955638416,"uuid":"a53b9f2a-8bef-4192-8256-be497af81082"}
